# CODEOWNERS — downstream org-config skeleton (placeholder).
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# This repo is org-admin-equivalent (it holds the App credentials and the config
# that rewrites org settings), so gate every admin-critical path with a required
# code-owner review. Replace @YOUR_ORG_ADMIN with this org's owner (a user or a
# team, e.g. @your-org/admins).
#
# NOTE (ADR-0006): on the GitHub Free plan a PRIVATE repo has no ENFORCEABLE
# branch protection or CODEOWNERS gate — this file is advisory until the org is
# on Team+. Keep it correct now so protection takes effect on upgrade.

/.github/                        @YOUR_ORG_ADMIN
/otterdog.json                   @YOUR_ORG_ADMIN
/otterdog/                       @YOUR_ORG_ADMIN
/secrets/                        @YOUR_ORG_ADMIN
/.sops.yaml                      @YOUR_ORG_ADMIN
/drift-allowlist.toml            @YOUR_ORG_ADMIN
